Extension API: select or deselect ONE ship in the open fleet box.

Adds `MSG_SELECT_SHIP` (0x85), client -> server: int16 ship_idx, uint8
selected (0 or 1). The command selects or deselects that ship in the
stack the fleet box shows, exactly as a human painting one icon cell
does — and nothing else. It is the WRITE half of full fleet control in
OrionLayer; open fix 20 (`doc/ext_fleet_selection.patch`) is the READ
half and stays as it is. Open fix 21 in doc/orion2re_open_fixes.md;
briefs 116 and 117.

STATUS: REPORTED, NOT APPLIED (15 September 2026). OrionLayer sends it
only while the snapshot carries open fix 20's "FSEL" block, and reads
the effect back off that block; an engine without this patch drops the
message in ProcessInput's `default:` and the cell simply does not change.

WHY A COMMAND (measured live, brief 116): the toggle cannot be reached
from outside today. `ACTIVATE_FIELD` on a ship field is not acted on
(mainscr.cpp:3422-3436), and an `INJECT_CLICK` on one did not toggle it:
the original paints the selection in the draw pass from the pointer
under a held button (mainscr_main.cpp:983-995,
MAINSCR::Set_Painted_Fleet_Fields_, mainscr.cpp:2468). ALL is the only
selection control a client can send.

WHAT THE HANDLER DOES — the checker, all of it before anything is written:
    * box 2 is open (MOVEBOX::Moveable_Box_Selected_(2));
    * _fleet_box_ship_stack is a stack that exists (< _ship_stack_count);
    * ship_idx is a ship (< _NUM_SHIPS), the local player owns it, and
      MAINSCR::Ship_Can_Be_Selected_ allows it — the same test the painted
      cell makes (it is HACCESS::Player_Can_Order_Ship_, so a ship in
      transit needs the communications tech, shipmove.cpp Can_Order_Ship_);
    * the ship is in that stack's node chain (walked from
      _ship_stack_start[stack], bounded by MAX_SHIPS; the side-effecting
      HACCESS::Node_Ptr_From_Ship_Stack_ is not used).
    Then, and only then: _ship_node[node].selected = selected, and the bit
    in _fleet_icon_selection_status that Save_Ship_Selection_Status_ keeps
    across a stack rebuild (fleetpop.cpp:356-375). A refused command
    changes nothing and draws nothing — no message box, so nothing can
    spin in ext::Tick the way open fix 12's refusals had to be kept from.

ONE DIFFERENCE FROM THE PAINTED CELL, stated: the command reaches a ship
that the box has scrolled out of its nine icons. Selecting it after
scrolling is the same state, so nothing the original could not reach is
reachable, only reachable without the scroll.

ORDER OF APPLICATION: independent of open fix 20. Both touch
src/ext/ext_api.cpp in different places (20 the end of SerializeState,
21 a new function before ProcessInput and a case inside it); verified
applying 20 then 21 and 21 then 20 on a copy of the tree.

